window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_c-5dc40968e1c15c37"]={"key":"ny_c-5dc40968e1c15c37","group":"ny_c","uid":"5dc40968e1c15c37","rank":44,"title":"orlebar court night actions card","occupation":"concierges","archetype":"authored_doc","subbatch":"corpus_c1","prompt":"You're covering the overnight handover at Orlebar Court for Astrid Lövgren at Sunderly Works. The building was handed over in July, the chief concierge left before handover, and Emil Sarkisian's colleague is alone on the desk from 22:00 to 06:00. I need one laminated A4 night-shift critical actions card in place before winter, for the first two minutes of anything going wrong. The unopened operations pack is 140 pages and there are eleven lever-arch files: it includes lift entrapment, sprinkler and gas isolation, smoke-vent override, alarm codes, the dry riser inlet and about forty contractor contacts, but two handover documents disagree about where the sprinkler isolation valve is. Use your judgement about what a lone person actually needs at 03:00, and make the unresolved valve location something the site team can verify before relying on the card. Edith Rivenburgh and Petra Fontaine will review it with Ashcombe Chambers, while Jelena Haldorsen, Jasmin Tanaka and Aneta Hargrove need to be able to use it without a facilities tutorial. Keep the card to one A4 page and roughly fifteen action lines; use plain, glanceable language, mark where specialist or emergency-service responsibility begins, and do not turn it into a directory or code table. Write `orlebar_court_night_actions_card.docx` into the top level of the working directory, using exactly that filename.\n\n---\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `orlebar_court_night_actions_card.docx` — A one-page, laminated-card-ready night-shift critical actions card for the lone concierge at Orlebar Court. (Exactly one A4 page when opened and rendered with the document's embedded settings.; Approximately fifteen concise action lines, with clear emergency escalation and specialist-responsibility boundaries.; Must be usable at a glance by a lone night concierge who is not a facilities specialist.; Must address the conflicting sprinkler-valve information through a verification or hold-point rather than an unsupported asserted location.; Must not become a tutorial, contractor directory, alarm-code table, or facilities maintenance procedure.; Write to the top level of the starting working directory with exactly the specified filename.)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/orlebar_court_night_actions_card.docx","bytes":39603,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/3c701d1894eb3635e02093638ff5699f92c3611a05a9a3887cd12d840601b99c.docx","sha256":"3c701d1894eb3635e02093638ff5699f92c3611a05a9a3887cd12d840601b99c","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"ORLEBAR COURT   |   NIGHT CONCIERGE • 22:00–06:00\nCRITICAL ACTIONS  •  FIRST TWO MINUTES\nSTOP • Protect yourself and others. Do not enter smoke, fire, gas, floodwater or any unsafe area.\n01  IMMEDIATE DANGER\nAssess first. Keep clear, make the area safe only if you can, and withdraw if control is unsafe.\n02  FIRE / SMOKE\nRaise the alarm and call 999/112. Follow the building fire plan and move people by a safe route; never investigate through smoke.\n03  LIFT — PERSON INSIDE\nEstablish two-way contact if safe; reassure and note the car/floor. Injury, distress, fire or danger → 999/112; otherwise use the approved lift specialist.\n04  LIFT — FAULT\nKeep people out and report it. Never force doors, climb out, reset equipment or attempt a technical rescue.\n05  GAS SMELL / RELEASE\nNo flames, smoking or electrical switching. Move people away; call 999/112 or the approved specialist. Do not find, diagnose or repair the leak.\n06  GAS ISOLATION\nOnly isolate if specifically authorised, safely accessible and within your competence; otherwise stop, withdraw and wait for competent help.\n07  SPRINKLER / WATER ESCAPE\nProtect occupants and contain spread only if safe and authorised. Do not improvise repairs or isolate fire protection while fire/smoke may be present unless directed by the responsible authority.\n08  DISPUTED SPRINKLER VALVE\nDo not rely on either handover record. Before lamination, physically verify valve identity/location against site labels with competent facilities staff.\n09  FLOOD / MAJOR LEAK\nMove people away; avoid switches and electrical equipment. Do not enter water where electrics may be affected; preserve responder access and escalate.\n10  POWER / SERVICES FAILURE\nUse a torch or approved emergency light (no candles/open flame). Check for immediate hazards, keep access clear, and call facilities/on-call.\n11  SMOKE-VENT CONTROL\nTreat as life-safety equipment. Use only under the approved emergency arrangement or competent direction; do not troubleshoot or improvise settings.\n12  SECURITY / FORCED ENTRY\nDo not confront or pursue. Keep yourself and others safe, secure distance, and call 999/112 for danger or suspicious activity; otherwise alert the manager.\n13  MEDICAL DISTRESS\nCall 999/112. Give basic first aid/AED only within your training; keep the casualty or vulnerable person reassured and attended where safe.\n14  ALARMS / RESPONDER ACCESS\nDo not reset, silence, isolate or disable an alarm to stop noise. Record the panel indication (never codes); keep desk/access route available. Dry-riser inlet is for responders—do not operate or test.\n15  CALL • LOG • HAND OVER\nFor help give: Orlebar Court + verified address/location, incident, casualties and hazards. Log time, location, condition, calls and actions; hand over facts to the incoming manager/responder.\n\nCONCIERGE SCOPE: Make safe • raise alarm • call • communicate • record. Fire-system, lift, gas, electrical and smoke-vent technical work, resets and life-safety isolation belong to competent specialists or emergency services. Keep away/stop work when unsafe. Do not speculate, assign blame, claim resolved, or promise an unconfirmed outcome.\nVERIFY BEFORE LAMINATION\nON-CALL (approved role/number)\nSPECIALIST (lift/life-safety)\nEmergency building address / responder location: ____________________\nSprinkler isolation valve ID / location (physically verified): ____________________\nBuilding manager / facilities: ____________________\nContact: ____________________\nCONTROL  Version: ______   Review date: ______   Verified by: ____________________   NOT VALID UNTIL LOCAL FIELDS ARE CHECKED","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"R01","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The submitted artifact is a readable DOCX with the exact required filename.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Filename and document opening.","grader_hint":"Confirm the top-level file is named exactly orlebar_court_night_actions_card.docx and opens without corruption."},{"rubric_item_id":"R02","check":"geometry","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The rendered card occupies no more than one A4 page.","weight":5.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered page count and paper size.","grader_hint":"Render with LibreOffice or an equivalent offline converter; confirm A4 dimensions and exactly one page."},{"rubric_item_id":"R03","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The card is compact enough to function as a roughly fifteen-line quick-reference rather than a prose manual.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Visible action-line count and density.","grader_hint":"Count the principal numbered or separated action lines; accept approximately 12-18 concise lines, excluding title and small local-fill fields."},{"rubric_item_id":"R04","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The visual hierarchy allows a lone worker to find the immediate action, escalation, and do-not-do warning within seconds.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered artifact.","grader_hint":"Judge scanability at normal A4 viewing size: distinct event labels, short action phrases, and visually prominent emergency escalation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R05","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The card identifies Orlebar Court and the night concierge or overnight desk context.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Header or context line.","grader_hint":"Look for Orlebar Court and a clear night/overnight concierge designation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R06","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The card tells the reader to assess immediate danger and personal safety before intervening.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"General opening instruction.","grader_hint":"Accept explicit wording about staying safe, not entering danger, and assessing whether evacuation or emergency services are needed."},{"rubric_item_id":"R07","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The card directs the concierge to call emergency services promptly for fire, serious injury, gas danger, or other immediate life threat.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Escalation instruction.","grader_hint":"Confirm emergency-service escalation is explicit and not hidden only in a general contacts list."},{"rubric_item_id":"R08","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The card uses a locally appropriate emergency number or an unmistakable emergency-services call instruction without inventing a building-specific number.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Emergency call line.","grader_hint":"Accept 999/112 if presented consistently with the apparent UK setting, or a clearly labeled emergency-services call instruction; reject fabricated property numbers."},{"rubric_item_id":"R09","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The card tells the lone concierge to give their location, the incident type, and known hazards when calling for help.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Call-information wording.","grader_hint":"Look for location/building, nature of incident, and hazard or casualty information."},{"rubric_item_id":"R10","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The card tells the concierge to keep the desk or access route available for responders where safe.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Responder-access instruction.","grader_hint":"Accept an instruction to facilitate responder access without requiring the concierge to leave a dangerous position."},{"rubric_item_id":"R11","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The card includes a fire or smoke action that prioritizes raising the alarm and emergency escalation over investigation.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Fire/smoke action line.","grader_hint":"Confirm alarm/emergency escalation comes before or alongside any safe limited check, not after searching the building."},{"rubric_item_id":"R12","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The fire or smoke instruction directs evacuation or movement away from danger in accordance with the building's established arrangements, without inventing a route.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Fire movement instruction.","grader_hint":"Accept wording to follow the building fire plan, use safe routes, and keep clear of smoke; do not require an invented assembly point."},{"rubric_item_id":"R13","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The card warns against entering smoke, fire, or another unsafe area to investigate or retrieve information.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Safety warning.","grader_hint":"Look for an explicit no-entry or do-not-risk-yourself warning."},{"rubric_item_id":"R14","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The card distinguishes a lift passenger entrapment from a lift fault and tells the concierge to establish communication with occupants if safe.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Lift incident line.","grader_hint":"Require both the entrapment distinction and safe reassurance/communication, not merely 'call lift company'."},{"rubric_item_id":"R15","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"For lift entrapment, the card directs emergency escalation when there is injury, distress, fire, or other urgent danger.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Lift escalation wording.","grader_hint":"Confirm urgent conditions trigger emergency services rather than waiting only for a contractor."},{"rubric_item_id":"R16","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The card tells the concierge not to force lift doors, climb out, or attempt a technical rescue.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Lift prohibition.","grader_hint":"Look for explicit prohibitions on door forcing, self-extraction assistance, or technical intervention."},{"rubric_item_id":"R17","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The card treats a gas smell or suspected gas release as an immediate hazard and directs avoidance of ignition sources and electrical switching.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Gas action line.","grader_hint":"Confirm no flames/smoking and no operating switches or equipment; accept concise equivalent language."},{"rubric_item_id":"R18","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The gas instruction tells the concierge to move people away and escalate to emergency or specialist help rather than diagnose the leak.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Gas evacuation/escalation wording.","grader_hint":"Require both moving away and escalation; reject instructions to locate or repair the leak."},{"rubric_item_id":"R19","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The card makes clear that gas isolation is only undertaken if specifically authorized, safely accessible, and within the concierge's competence.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Gas boundary wording.","grader_hint":"Look for a conditional boundary, not an unconditional instruction to operate the gas valve."},{"rubric_item_id":"R20","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The card identifies a sprinkler discharge or water escape as requiring occupant safety, isolation only where safe and authorized, and escalation.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Water/sprinkler action line.","grader_hint":"Confirm the line covers safety, controlled escalation, and does not invite improvised repair."},{"rubric_item_id":"R21","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The card explicitly separates sprinkler isolation from fire response and warns not to isolate or disable protection while fire or smoke may be present unless directed by the responsible authority.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Sprinkler safety boundary.","grader_hint":"Require the conflict between stopping water and preserving fire protection to be handled explicitly."},{"rubric_item_id":"R22","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The card does not assert an unverified sprinkler isolation-valve location.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Sprinkler location text.","grader_hint":"Search for a definite location claim; credit only if the card uses a verified field or conditional wording rather than choosing one conflicting record."},{"rubric_item_id":"R23","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The card requires the sprinkler-valve location and identification to be physically verified against site labeling or a competent facilities check before the card is relied upon.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Verification hold-point.","grader_hint":"Look for an explicit pre-publication/site-verification instruction tied to the disputed valve."},{"rubric_item_id":"R24","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The card provides a clearly labeled place to record the verified sprinkler-valve location or identification.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Local-fill field.","grader_hint":"Accept a labeled blank such as 'verified sprinkler isolation valve/location'; do not require a fabricated value."},{"rubric_item_id":"R25","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The card treats smoke-vent controls as life-safety equipment and directs the concierge to use them only under the building's approved emergency arrangement or competent direction.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Smoke-vent line.","grader_hint":"Require conditional, controlled use rather than a generic instruction to press an override."},{"rubric_item_id":"R26","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The smoke-vent instruction does not tell the concierge to improvise a ventilation setting or troubleshoot the control system.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Smoke-vent boundary.","grader_hint":"Reject diagnostic or repair directions and credit a clear stop/escalate boundary."},{"rubric_item_id":"R27","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The card includes a general power failure or building-services failure response that preserves personal safety, checks for immediate hazards, and escalates the outage.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Power/services line.","grader_hint":"Look for safe lighting/access awareness, hazard check, and reporting/escalation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R28","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The card tells the concierge to use a torch or other safe means of seeing during an outage and not to use candles or open flame.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Outage safety wording.","grader_hint":"Accept torch/approved emergency lighting plus an open-flame prohibition."},{"rubric_item_id":"R29","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The card includes a flooding or major leak response that avoids electrical hazards and moves people away from affected areas.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Flood/leak line.","grader_hint":"Require both electrical caution and area control or movement away."},{"rubric_item_id":"R30","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The card instructs the concierge to preserve access and avoid entering water where electrical equipment may be affected.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Flood boundary.","grader_hint":"Look for an explicit no-entry/electrical-risk condition."},{"rubric_item_id":"R31","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The card includes a security or forced-entry response that prioritizes personal safety, avoids confrontation, and escalates suspicious or dangerous activity.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Security incident line.","grader_hint":"Require non-confrontation and escalation, not a security-investigation procedure."},{"rubric_item_id":"R32","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The card provides a response for a person in medical distress that directs emergency escalation and basic assistance only within the concierge's training.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Medical incident line.","grader_hint":"Accept emergency call, first aid/AED if trained, and no unsupported clinical instruction."},{"rubric_item_id":"R33","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The card tells the concierge to keep a casualty or vulnerable person attended to or reassured while waiting, where safe.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Medical support wording.","grader_hint":"Look for safe reassurance/monitoring without overclaiming treatment authority."},{"rubric_item_id":"R34","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The card includes a dry-riser reference only as a responder-access or location aid, not as equipment the concierge should operate or test.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Dry-riser wording.","grader_hint":"Credit a concise dry-riser inlet location field or responder note paired with a no-operation boundary."},{"rubric_item_id":"R35","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The card tells the concierge not to reset, silence, isolate, or disable an alarm merely to stop noise or clear a panel.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Alarm boundary.","grader_hint":"Require an explicit prohibition against casual alarm reset/silencing/isolation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R36","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The card directs the concierge to record the alarm panel indication or incident details without exposing or reproducing alarm codes.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Alarm recording instruction.","grader_hint":"Look for indication/event recording and a clear code confidentiality or no-code-table boundary."},{"rubric_item_id":"R37","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The card provides one concise escalation path to the building manager or designated facilities/on-call function for non-immediate technical support.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Escalation field.","grader_hint":"Accept a labeled local-fill on-call contact field; do not require invented names or numbers."},{"rubric_item_id":"R38","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The escalation path distinguishes emergency services from the building manager/facilities function.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Contact hierarchy.","grader_hint":"Confirm urgent life-safety calls are not routed first to a manager or contractor."},{"rubric_item_id":"R39","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The card includes a clearly labeled local-fill field for the verified emergency building address or responder location information.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Local information field.","grader_hint":"Credit a blank field rather than a made-up address."},{"rubric_item_id":"R40","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The card includes a clearly labeled local-fill field for the approved building on-call contact.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Local information field.","grader_hint":"Accept role/contact placeholder; reject a fabricated personal number."},{"rubric_item_id":"R41","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The card includes a clearly labeled local-fill field for the approved lift or life-safety specialist contact, without listing a directory.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Specialist contact field.","grader_hint":"One or two role-based fields are acceptable; a broad contact list is not."},{"rubric_item_id":"R42","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The card states that the concierge may make the area safe, raise the alarm, call help, and communicate observations, but does not authorize specialist repair or investigation.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Role boundary statement.","grader_hint":"Look for a positive concierge scope and an explicit boundary, not merely a generic disclaimer."},{"rubric_item_id":"R43","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The card marks fire-system, lift, gas, electrical, and smoke-vent technical work as belonging to competent specialists or emergency services.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Function-boundary wording.","grader_hint":"Require the major specialist domains to be covered collectively; do not require separate paragraphs."},{"rubric_item_id":"R44","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The card tells the concierge to communicate the incident and actions taken to the incoming manager or responder at handover.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Handover line.","grader_hint":"Look for concise incident handover or log instruction."},{"rubric_item_id":"R45","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The card requires factual incident logging including time, location, observed condition, calls made, and actions taken.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Logging instruction.","grader_hint":"Credit a compact record checklist containing all five factual elements."},{"rubric_item_id":"R46","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The card warns the reader not to speculate about cause, assign blame, or claim that a hazard is resolved without confirmation.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Reporting boundary.","grader_hint":"Look for factual-only reporting and no unsupported closure claim."},{"rubric_item_id":"R47","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The card uses action verbs and short phrases suitable for a stressed reader rather than explanatory paragraphs.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered text.","grader_hint":"Judge whether most lines can be acted on without reading background explanation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R48","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The wording is understandable to a new or cross-functional reader without turning the card into a tutorial.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered artifact.","grader_hint":"Judge plain language, limited jargon, and sufficient context for action without background lessons."},{"rubric_item_id":"R49","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Any unavoidable technical term such as dry riser, smoke vent, or sprinkler isolation is paired with enough action context to prevent misuse.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Technical labels in context.","grader_hint":"Reject unexplained equipment names presented as if the reader should operate them."},{"rubric_item_id":"R50","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The card contains a clear instruction to keep away from or stop work around a hazard when the concierge cannot safely control it.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"General stop-work wording.","grader_hint":"Look for a repeatable stop/withdraw/escalate principle."},{"rubric_item_id":"R51","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The card tells the concierge to avoid promising residents, contractors, or responders an outcome that has not been confirmed.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Communication boundary.","grader_hint":"Accept no promises/no unsupported reassurance wording."},{"rubric_item_id":"R52","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The card does not require the lone concierge to leave the desk unattended for a nonessential information-gathering task during an active emergency.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Action sequencing and scope.","grader_hint":"Judge whether directions preserve the lone worker's ability to call, monitor, and receive responders."},{"rubric_item_id":"R53","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The card presents a defensible priority order: protect people, summon appropriate help, communicate essential facts, then perform only safe bounded checks or controls.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Overall sequence.","grader_hint":"Assess the whole card for priority logic rather than requiring a particular numbering scheme."},{"rubric_item_id":"R54","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The card distinguishes information to verify before publication from actions that can be taken immediately during an incident.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Verification and incident wording.","grader_hint":"Confirm the disputed valve and local contacts are visibly marked as pre-use/site-verification items, not presented as live incident instructions."},{"rubric_item_id":"R55","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The card has a visible version, review, or verification marker so the site team can identify whether local fields have been checked before lamination.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Footer or control field.","grader_hint":"Accept a version/date/verified-by field; it need not contain a fabricated date or person."},{"rubric_item_id":"R56","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The final artifact is operationally credible: a night concierge can identify what to do, what not to do, and whom to call for each major scenario without asking the author a question.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Whole rendered card.","grader_hint":"Judge practical completeness across fire/smoke, lift entrapment, gas, sprinkler/water, outage, security, medical distress, and escalation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R57","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The card omits a broad contractor directory, forty-number contact dump, or full alarm-code table and instead uses only role-based local-fill escalation fields.","weight":-5.0,"polarity":"penalty","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered card contents.","grader_hint":"Apply the penalty if the card reproduces or attempts to summarize the contractor directory or alarm-code tables, or becomes materially longer because of them."},{"rubric_item_id":"R58","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The card does not end with a vague 'follow up later' or multi-option next-steps list; it ends with an actionable stop, handover, or record instruction.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Final visible line.","grader_hint":"Inspect the ending: it should close on a concrete immediate action or controlled handover, not an unresolved menu of future tasks."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"This is a residential-building concierge handover artifact for a regional property operation. It is an instructional, reusable emergency-reference card intended for a lone overnight desk worker and reviewed by internal stakeholders before controlled site use.","difficulty_sources":["Selecting immediate life-safety actions from broad facilities knowledge without turning the card into a manual","Making the card usable by a lone concierge while marking the boundary between concierge actions and specialist or emergency-service work","Handling conflicting handover information about the sprinkler isolation valve without inventing a location","Compressing dependent actions, warnings, escalation points, and local fields into a genuinely usable one-page card"],"authoring_plan":{"artifact":"Create one polished DOCX card for Orlebar Court, set to A4 and constrained to one rendered page. Use a compact title, a highly scannable set of approximately fifteen action lines, and small labeled local-fill/control fields. Keep the text suitable for lamination and avoid explanatory paragraphs.","content_constraints":["The card must be usable by one person at 03:00: first protect self and others, call emergency services for immediate danger, communicate location and hazards, then perform only safe bounded actions.","Cover fire/smoke, lift entrapment, gas smell/release, sprinkler discharge or water escape, smoke-vent controls, power/building-services failure, security/forced entry, medical distress, dry-riser responder information, escalation, and incident logging.","For fire and smoke, prioritize alarm, emergency escalation, safe evacuation/movement, and no entry into smoke or fire.","For lift entrapment, establish safe communication, reassure, escalate urgently for injury/distress/fire, and never force doors or attempt a technical rescue.","For gas, avoid ignition and electrical switching, move people away, call appropriate help, and never diagnose or repair. Gas isolation is conditional on authorization, safe access, and competence.","For sprinkler discharge, preserve fire protection where fire or smoke may exist; isolation is not an automatic concierge action. The disputed valve location must be explicitly held for physical/site verification and represented with a blank or controlled field, never guessed.","For smoke vents, say that use follows the approved emergency arrangement or competent direction; do not provide troubleshooting or improvised settings.","For outages and flooding, preserve visibility, avoid open flame and electrical hazards, move people away from unsafe areas, and escalate.","For security and medical events, avoid confrontation, summon emergency help where needed, provide only trained assistance, and keep a casualty or vulnerable person reassured where safe.","Include role-based escalation fields for emergency services, building manager/facilities on-call, and lift/life-safety specialist. Do not invent phone numbers or addresses.","Include a concise factual incident-log reminder covering time, location, observed condition, calls, and actions, plus handover.","Mark the concierge's boundary: make safe, raise alarm, call, communicate, and record; specialist repair, technical investigation, system reset, and life-safety isolation belong to competent specialists or emergency services.","Use plain language for mixed-background readers but do not turn the card into a lesson. Include a version/review/verified-by control field so local checks can be completed before lamination."],"derived_gold_relationships":["The sprinkler-location field must remain blank, conditional, or explicitly subject to site verification; any definite unsupported location fails the key ambiguity-handling requirement.","Emergency-service escalation must be more prominent and earlier in priority than contractor or manager escalation when life safety is at stake.","Technical controls are subordinate to safety and authority: no automatic gas, sprinkler, smoke-vent, alarm, lift, or electrical intervention.","The artifact should fit about fifteen principal action lines by combining related actions carefully, not by deleting the scenarios or replacing them with generic 'call someone' language.","Local facts unavailable from supplied materials must be represented as labeled blanks or verification points, not invented values.","The single over-production penalty targets reproducing the forty contractor numbers or alarm-code tables; the gold should show that role-based escalation is sufficient for this card."],"review_focus":["Render and inspect page count, A4 geometry, readability, and whether action lines remain glanceable.","Check all major incident categories and the safe/unsafe boundaries independently.","Check that mixed-background readers can act without a tutorial and that the card does not authorize facilities work owned by another function.","Check the last line is a concrete handover/log/stop action rather than an open-ended next-steps list."]},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"primary_plus_appendix","structure":"strict_schema"},"reference_files":[],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"night_actions_card","filename":"orlebar_court_night_actions_card.docx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","description":"A one-page, laminated-card-ready night-shift critical actions card for the lone concierge at Orlebar Court.","required":true,"constraints":["Exactly one A4 page when opened and rendered with the document's embedded settings.","Approximately fifteen concise action lines, with clear emergency escalation and specialist-responsibility boundaries.","Must be usable at a glance by a lone night concierge who is not a facilities specialist.","Must address the conflicting sprinkler-valve information through a verification or hold-point rather than an unsupported asserted location.","Must not become a tutorial, contractor directory, alarm-code table, or facilities maintenance procedure.","Write to the top level of the starting working directory with exactly the specified filename."],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"communicate_stakeholders","work_product":"form_or_template","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"closed_world_with_assumptions"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"authored_doc@v4","occupation":"concierges","sector":"real_estate_rental_leasing","task_archetype":"authored_doc","estimated_professional_hours":2.5,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"hybrid","reviewer_policy":"Have an independent document reviewer render the DOCX offline, verify the one-page geometry and compactness, then have a property-operations reviewer assess the emergency priorities, specialist boundaries, disputed-valve hold-point, and usability for a lone overnight concierge. Penalize unsupported local facts and over-production.","minimum_reviewers":2,"known_limitations":["No handover files or building-specific contact data are supplied, so the gold should use clearly labeled verification or local-fill fields rather than asserting an address, phone number, valve location, alarm code, or contractor identity.","The rubric evaluates occupationally defensible emergency-reference content, not compliance certification or jurisdiction-specific fire-engineering advice."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"结构/材料验收记录","detail":"validated 属于结构、防泄漏、材料推进验收；没有内容正确率结论。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-24T13:43:36+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-24T13:43:36+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-24T13:43:36+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-24T13:43:36+00:00"},{"check":"instruction_rubric_overlap","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":false,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-24T13:43:36+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_c1/runs/5dc40968e1c15c37","declared_deliverables":["orlebar_court_night_actions_card.docx"]};
